@document
  title: Inline Formatting Test Corpus
  allow_undefined: true

@meta
  author: LDOC Test Suite
  version: 1.0
  company: Acme Corp
  nested:
    value: deep
  items: ["first", "second", "third"]

# Text Emphasis

This paragraph demonstrates **bold text** using double asterisks.

This paragraph demonstrates __bold text__ using double underscores.

This paragraph demonstrates *italic text* using single asterisks.

This paragraph demonstrates _italic text_ using single underscores.

This paragraph demonstrates ***bold and italic*** using triple asterisks.

This paragraph demonstrates ~~strikethrough text~~ using double tildes.

Combining styles: **bold with *nested italic* inside** and *italic with **nested bold** inside*.

# Inline Code

Use the `console.log()` function to print output.

The `{{variable}}` syntax is used for variable interpolation.

Multiple code spans: `const x = 1` and `let y = 2` on the same line.

# Links

Here is a [basic link](https://example.com) to an external site.

Here is a [link with title](https://example.com "Example Site Title") that shows on hover.

Multiple links: [first](https://one.com) and [second](https://two.com) in one paragraph.

Relative link: [local page](./other-document.ldoc) for internal references.

# Images

Basic image: ![Company Logo](images/logo.png)

Image with title: ![Product Photo](images/product.jpg "Our flagship product")

Image with empty alt: ![](images/decorative.png)

# Cross-References

See [[Section Name]] for more details.

Refer to [[anchor-name]] defined elsewhere in the document.

See also [[Text Emphasis]] above and [[Footnotes]] below.

# Defined Terms

The term "Confidential Information" means all non-public data.

When we say "Agreement" we refer to this entire document.

The "Effective Date" shall be the date of last signature.

# Footnotes

This statement requires a citation[^1] for verification.

Multiple footnotes[^2] can appear[^note] in the same paragraph.

A footnote with a descriptive label[^legal-disclaimer] is also valid.

[^1]: This is the first footnote definition.
[^2]: This is the second footnote with more detail.
[^note]: Named footnotes improve readability.
[^legal-disclaimer]: This document does not constitute legal advice.

# Variables

Simple variable: {{author}} wrote this document.

Nested path: {{nested.value}} accesses deep properties.

Array access: {{items.0}} gets the first item.

Variable with filter: {{company | uppercase}} transforms the value.

Multiple filters: {{author | trim | lowercase}} chains transformations.

Conditional display: Version {{version}} is current.

# Blanks and Placeholders

Please sign here: _____

The buyer, __________, agrees to the terms.

Date: _____ / _____ / _____

Fill in the blank: The capital of France is __________.

# Hard Line Breaks

This line ends with two spaces  
and continues on the next line without a paragraph break.

This line ends with a backslash\
and also continues without a paragraph break.

Normal paragraph break requires a blank line.

Like this one.

# Combined Examples

The **"Confidential Information"** (as defined in [[Definitions]]) includes `source code`[^code-def].

Please sign below: _____ and visit [our website](https://example.com) for more info.

Contact {{author}} at *{{company}}* for questions about **{{version}}**.

[^code-def]: Source code includes all human-readable programming instructions.
